# Burn Engine servings & food-list gram weights

Complete agent reference for Burn & Build serving math. **Do not re-read `js/burnEngine.js` for basics** — use this doc. Source of truth for code: `js/burnEngine.js` `computeServingsPhase`.

This system is **not** straight calorie/macro counting. The engine builds a plan once; the user follows **servings** and weighs food to **gram portions** on the approved list.

## Core principle

**A serving is defined by grams of the target macro, with a fat ceiling in grams — not by calories.**

| Wrong | Right |
|-------|-------|
| “32 calories of protein per serving” | **8g protein** per serving, **≤2g fat** |
| “56 calories of carbs per grain serving” | **14g carbs** per serving |
| “40 calories of vegetables” | **10g carbs** per serving |
| Weigh food without knowing prep state | Gram weight only valid for the **labeled prep** (dry / cooked / raw) |

The engine’s balancing loops use **calorie weights** internally (32, 56, 40, 72, 45…). **Food-list portion sizing uses macro grams + fat limits.** Calories in loops are plumbing; users follow servings and gram weights.

---

## Engine slots → user-facing servings

`computeServingsPhase` uses **seven internal slots**. The Servings page shows **six user-facing numbers** (some slots are merged).

| Engine slot | Variable | User-facing field | Combined? |
|-------------|----------|-------------------|-----------|
| Non-dairy protein | `P1` | `servings.protein` | **Yes** — merged with `D1` |
| Dairy protein | `D1` | ↑ same row | **Yes** — merged with `P1` |
| Grains | `G1` | `servings.grainsStarches` | **Yes** — merged with `S2` |
| Starches | `S2` | ↑ same row | **Yes** — merged with `G1` |
| Vegetables | `VE` | `servings.vegetables` | No — always **1** |
| Fruits | `FQ` | `servings.fruits` | No — minimum **3** |
| Extra fat | `FT` | `servings.fatMaintain` | No |
| *(reduce fat)* | — | `servings.fatReduce` | Always **0** in current engine |

**Merged output formulas** (`js/burnEngine.js`):

- `protein` = `round(P1 + D1)` — at work intensity `4.0`, `round((P1 + D1) × 1.5)`
- `grainsStarches` = `round(G1 + S2)`
- `vegetables` = `1` (hard-coded)
- `fruits` = `round(FQ)` — engine enforces `FQ ≥ 3`
- `fatMaintain` = `round(FT)`
- `fatReduce` = `0`

**Special engine rules:**

- If `VE > 1` before cap: extra vegetable servings convert to **grain** servings (`G1` increases); `VE` is capped at **1**.
- `FQ` can be bumped up in the total-calorie reconciliation loop if the plan runs short.

