## All food categories — portion criteria

Use these to size **base** one-serving `gramWeight` in `data/foods.json` and `data/cuttingStaplesPrintout.js`. PDF food-list pages scale these by the user’s plan (see [PDF scaling](#pdf--printout-system) below).

### 1. Non-dairy protein (`P1`)

**Foods:** Meat, fish, seafood, egg whites. Category `protein` in `foods.json`.  
**Counts toward:** `servings.protein` (with dairy).

| Macro | Per one serving |
|-------|-----------------|
| **Protein** | **8g** |
| **Fat** | **≤2g** |

| Detail | Value |
|--------|-------|
| Screening rule | **8/2** (“eight-two”) |
| Gram formula | `800 ÷ protein_per_100g`, verify fat ≤ 2g at that weight |
| Seminar override | **1982 tested weights override USDA** when they differ |
| Engine protein loop | 32 cal/serving (= 8g × 4) |
| Engine fat loop | 18 cal/serving baked in (= 2g × 9) |
| Meal split | Daily total ÷ 3 → breakfast, lunch, dinner |
| Prep | Usually **cooked** (measure after cooking) |
| Audit | `scripts/protein-82-audit.mjs`, `scripts/protein-82-bodybuilder-audit.mjs` |

---

### 2. Dairy (`D1`)

**Foods:** Milk, yogurt, cottage cheese, ricotta. Category `dairy` in `foods.json`. Listed with protein on KWarner food-list page 5 (`CUTTING_STAPLES_PROTEIN_DAIRY`).  
**Counts toward:** `servings.protein` (same daily total as meat/fish — **not** a separate Servings row).

Dairy is a **compound serving** in the engine — one dairy serving carries protein, carbs, and fat budgets simultaneously:

| Macro | Per one dairy serving (`D1`) |
|-------|-------------------------------|
| **Protein** | **8g equivalent** (32 cal in protein loop) |
| **Carbs** | **12g** (48 cal in carb loop) |
| **Fat** | **~2.4g** (22 cal in fat loop) |

| Detail | Value |
|--------|-------|
| Gram formula | **Curated per item** — do not use the meat `800/protein` formula blindly |
| Product guidance | At least **one-third of daily protein from dairy** (`data/forBestResultsPrintout.js`) |
| Engine protein loop | 32 cal/serving (same slot weight as `P1`) |
| Engine carb loop | 48 cal/serving |
| Engine fat loop | 22 cal/serving |
| Meal split | Same as protein — counts toward daily protein ÷ 3 per meal |
| PDF food-list scale | `planServings.protein / 3` (same multiplier as meat) |
| Tips | `data/proteinTipsPrintout.js` — dairy column on protein food list |

---

### 3. Grains (`G1`)

**Foods:** Bread, oats, rice, pasta, cereal, tortillas, popcorn, etc. Category `grain` in `foods.json`.  
**Counts toward:** `servings.grainsStarches` (with starches).

| Macro | Per one serving |
|-------|-----------------|
| **Carbs** | **14g** |
| **Fat** | **≤1.0g** (“**14/1**”) |

| Detail | Value |
|--------|-------|
| Gram formula | `1400 ÷ carbs_per_100g` |
| Engine carb loop | 56 cal/serving (= 14g × 4) |
| Engine fat loop | 9 cal/serving baked in (~1g fat) |
| Engine protein loop | 3 cal/serving from grains (fat calories counted in protein reconciliation) |
| Meal split | Daily total ÷ 3 → breakfast, lunch, dinner |
| Prep — **dry** | Oats, grits, farina, cream of wheat — weigh **dry**; user adds water |
| Prep — **cooked** | Rice, pasta, quinoa — weigh **cooked** |
| Prep — **as-is** | Bread, bagels, rice cakes, tortillas |
| Audit | `scripts/grains-14-1-audit.mjs`, `scripts/grains-82-audit.mjs` |
| Handbook | Bread **1 oz** per serving — measure slices |

---

### 4. Starches (`S2`)

**Foods:** Beans, potatoes, sweet potatoes, corn, peas, squash, lentils. Category `starch` in `foods.json`.  
**Counts toward:** `servings.grainsStarches` (with grains).

| Macro | Per one serving |
|-------|-----------------|
| **Carbs** | **14g** |
| **Fat** | **≤0.44g** (“**14/0.44**”) |

| Detail | Value |
|--------|-------|
| Gram formula | `1400 ÷ carbs_per_100g` |
| Engine carb loop | 56 cal/serving (= 14g × 4) — **same carb target as grains** |
| Engine fat loop | 4 cal/serving baked in (~0.44g fat) — **stricter than grains** |
| Engine protein loop | 3 cal/serving (with grains) |
| Meal split | Daily total ÷ 3 → breakfast, lunch, dinner |
| Prep | Mostly **cooked**; some squash entries use **raw** weights in catalog |
| Audit | `scripts/starches-14-0-audit.mjs`, `scripts/starches-82-audit.mjs` |
| Note | Beans/rice count here as **starches/grains**, not protein (`data/grainsStarchesTipsPrintout.js`) |

**Why grains and starches are separate internally:** Same **14g carb** target, different **fat ceilings** (1.0g vs 0.44g). User sees one combined number; agents must use the correct slot when sizing portions.

---

### 5. Vegetables (`VE`)

**Foods:** Broccoli, peppers, mushrooms, spinach, etc. Category `vegetable` in `foods.json`.  
**Counts toward:** `servings.vegetables` — always **1** daily on every plan.

| Macro | Per one serving |
|-------|-----------------|
| **Carbs** | **10g** |
| **Fat** | **≤3g** |

| Detail | Value |
|--------|-------|
| Gram formula | `1000 ÷ carbs_per_100g` |
| Engine carb loop | 40 cal/serving (= 10g × 4) |
| Engine fat loop | 3 cal/serving baked in (~0.33g) |
| Meal placement | All daily vegetable servings at **dinner** (`generateMealSlots`) |
| Prep | **Raw and cooked are separate catalog rows** — never interchange |
| Measure rule | **After cooking** when cooked (`data/vegetableTipsPrintout.js`) |
| Audit | `scripts/veg-fruit-audit.mjs` |
| Engine cap | `VE` capped at 1; excess converts to grain (`G1`) servings |

---

### 6. Fruits (`FQ`)

**Foods:** Apples, bananas, berries, etc. Category `fruit` in `foods.json`.  
**Counts toward:** `servings.fruits` — minimum **3** daily.

| Macro | Per one serving |
|-------|-----------------|
| **Energy** | **72 calories** (engine fruit slot — carb-loop uses cal, not a fixed carb gram target) |
| **Fat** | **≤4g** at the portion |

| Detail | Value |
|--------|-------|
| Gram formula | `7200 ÷ kcal_per_100g` (calorie-density based) |
| Engine carb loop | 72 cal/serving |
| Engine fat loop | 4 cal/serving baked in (~0.44g) — grouped with `S2` in fat accounting |
| Meal split | Daily total ÷ 3 → morning snack, afternoon snack, evening snack |
| Prep | Usually **raw** |
| Audit | `scripts/veg-fruit-audit.mjs` |
| User rule | User follows **fruit servings**, not calories — do not expose calorie counting in UI |

---

### 7. Extra fat, sugar & alcohol (`FT`)

**Foods:** Category `fat`, `sugar`, or `alcohol` in `foods.json`. Planner label: **“Fat Points”** / **“Extra fat, sugar and alcohol”** (`EXTRA_FATS_LABEL` in `js/servingsPrintout.js`).  
**Counts toward:** `servings.fatMaintain` on Servings page. `servings.fatReduce` is always **0** in current engine.

| Macro | Per one point (`FT`) |
|-------|---------------------|
| **Energy** | **45 calories** (`FAT_SERVING_CALORIES`) |
| **Fat** | ~**5g** if pure fat (45 ÷ 9) — actual food portions are **curated per item** |

| Detail | Value |
|--------|-------|
| Engine fat loop | `FT × 45` cal added to total |
| Planner slot | Optional **fat** lane on breakfast/lunch/dinner meals (`TEMPLATE_SLOTS.meal`) |
| Planner categories | `fat`, `sugar`, `alcohol` share one point pool (`plannerState.js` `SLOT_META.fat`) |
| Portion sizing | Per-food **curated** in `foods.json` — grams (e.g. butter 6g/tsp) or descriptive units (e.g. `12 fl. oz.` beer, `2 inch-square` brownie) when `gramWeight` is 0 |
| Food-list PDF | **Not** on KWarner staple gram pages — fat/sugar/alcohol are planner/catalog foods, not cutting-staples rows |
| Unused points | `fatLossPoundsFromDailyServings()` — unused fat points → body-fat loss calc |

**Sub-lanes in menu planner** (`FAT_LANE_SLOT_LABELS`): Fat · Sugar · Alcohol — all draw from the same `fatMaintain` daily total.

