## Why prep state matters

| Prep | Examples | Rule |
|------|----------|------|
| **dry** | Oatmeal, grits, farina | Weigh **dry**; user adds water |
| **cooked** | Rice, pasta, mushrooms, broccoli | Weigh **after cooking** |
| **raw** | Cucumber, fruit, some salads | Eaten as-is |
| **as-is** | Bread, cottage cheese, milk | Product form |

Cooking changes water content → carbs/protein per 100g change → **different gram weights** for the same macro serving. **Never interchange** raw and cooked rows.

---

## Meal & snack distribution

From `generateMealSlots` / `js/servingsPrintout.js`:

| Group | Daily total split |
|-------|-------------------|
| Protein (+ dairy) | ÷ 3 → breakfast, lunch, dinner |
| Grains & starches | ÷ 3 → breakfast, lunch, dinner |
| Vegetables | **All at dinner** |
| Fruits | ÷ 3 → three snack slots |
| Extra fat | **Not** in servings grid — total `fatMaintain` only; optional per meal in planner |

Remainder distribution (e.g. 10 protein → 3, 4, 3): extras go to **lunch**, then **dinner** — not breakfast.

